    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup construction prioritizes high-upside matchups against mediocre arms, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (74.99) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.93). **Corbin Carroll** remains a foundational start despite a minor drag from the opposing battery's hold efficiency, as his elite sprint speed and favorable platoon advantage against Ryan Gusto provide the highest floor/ceiling combination on the team. **Seiya Suzuki** is similarly positioned for success; he benefits from an elite 19% boost due to the favorable SP matchup against JR Ritchie, combined with the structural value of hitting in the two-hole. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (68.46) also grades out as a premier play, with a 14% platoon-driven efficiency surge that makes him an essential piece against Cristian Javier.\n\nWe are navigating several complex decisions, most notably the exclusion of **Austin Riley** (52.47). While **Austin Riley** sits just outside our threshold for a \"Strong\" start, he remains the most difficult sit on the bench. Ultimately, his matchup against a high-tier arm in Shota Imanaga and the negative drift caused by the platoon disadvantage tipped the optimizer toward favoring the higher efficiency scores found in **Mickey Moniak** (66.02) and **Griffin Conine** (60.91). **Mickey Moniak** serves as a strategic play today; despite a significant platoon penalty against the southpaw, the 14% park factor and the 19% SP skill boost create a profile that outweighs the risks of his negative split.\n\nInvestors should remain alert to the risks inherent in today's \"Lineup Pending\" designations, as nearly every slot relies on projected batting orders that could shift our efficiency calculations. **James Wood** (51.80) is a notable high-variance start; while he is anchored by a stellar 0.413 xwOBA and a prime leadoff spot, he faces the formidable Zack Wheeler. Any late-breaking news on lineup changes\u2014particularly for **Gabriel Moreno** or **Brice Turang**\u2014could trigger an immediate re-evaluation of our efficiency rankings. We are currently comfortable with these selections, provided the weather holds and our projected order assumptions remain intact.",
